<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Nedcor H1 EPS, div rise 24 pct.</title>
<headline>Nedcor H1 EPS, div rise 24 pct.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half yr ended March 31</p>
<p>		(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		    261	     vs 210</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		    56		vs 45</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters expected Nedcor earnings to be in a range of 256.2 to 264.6 cents with consensus at 261.3. They put the dividend at between 54 and 56.7 cents, averaging out at 55.4 cents.</p>
<p>    Net income		   575	     vs 450</p>
<p>    Net interest income	1,618	   vs 1,391</p>
<p>    Non-interest revenue     1,125	   vs 938</p>
<p>Specific and general</p>
<p>	risk provisions	  187	     vs 149</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			857	     vs 718</p>
<p>    Tax			    282	     vs 268</p>
<p>Div payable</p>
<p>On register May 30</p>
<p>Full name: Nedcor Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said it would offer a capitalisation share award to ordinary shareholders. Terms of the cap award will be announced on May 26.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
